    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with significant firepower at the top of the order. Our premier play is **Yordan Alvarez** (82.49), who benefits from an elite xwOBA of 0.476 against Junk; his combination of raw power and a favorable matchup creates our highest upside. Closely trailing him is **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13), whose projection is bolstered by an assumed leadoff spot and a strong 14% boost from his platoon advantage against Flaherty. We also see high-ceiling production from **Christian Yelich** (74.24), who is prioritized today not just for his hitting profile, but for his stolen base potential; his matchup against Peralta\u2014who has a slow delivery\u2014elevates his stolen base probability to 92%, making him essential in our strategy to address the scarcity of the category. **Colt Keith** (69.64) rounds out the top tier, benefiting significantly from a wind-aided park factor and an assumed middle-of-the-order role against Taillon.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Nelson Velazquez**, who fell just short of our rotation with a 51.28 efficiency score. While his xwOBA of 0.394 is impressive, the optimizer favored **Lars Nootbaar** and the defensive versatility of the current starting configuration. We are closely monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for several key pieces, including **Dillon Dingler** and **Colt Keith**; should their official batting positions slide down the order, their efficiency scores will require immediate re-evaluation. While **Junior Caminero** (56.77) faces a stiff test against Cease, his pedigree keeps him in the lineup despite a 19% penalty for the opposing pitcher's elite skill set. Conversely, **Chase Meidroth** (34.47) was an easy exclusion, as facing deGrom drops his utility well below our 40.0 floor, and **Hyeseong Kim** remains unavailable as he continues his assignment with the Oklahoma City Comets.",
